  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (0.48-0.52) over image-only (0.21), and among RNA encoders, scvi_n200 (0.520) beats pca_n2000 (0.485) by ~3.5%. However, the scgpt foundation-model encoder is completely untested. Question: config_007 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_004, isolating the effect of encoder choice (scgpt vs scvi_n200) while holding profile setting and modality constant. Why this is best: Establishing the encoder hierarchy is the highest-priority design decision because the chosen encoder will underpin all subsequent multiprofile and multimodal experiments. If scgpt substantially outperforms scvi_n200, it becomes the backbone for the remaining 6 experiments; if it does not, we can confidently anchor on scvi_n200 and pivot to testing profile/aggregation/fusion. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful design axis before committing budget to more complex configurations."
}

